Z||000065||kslish||12-03-2000||08:26 AM||||My '86 4-cyl Coupe: "Frankenstein" (my first Fiero)<P>Named it that because I assembled it on an '86 chassis with parts from every year Fiero (depending on what ones I liked best or what was found at the parts yard at the time).  For example, since it had front end damage when I purchased it I had the bent frame cross-members cut out (everything from the headlights forward) and replaced with ones welded in from a junked '84.  The most obvious change is the '88 Formula facias on the front and rear....always liked the style of those, other changes too numerous to mention right now.<P>-----<P>My newest Fiero (got it 6 months ago): "The Pheonix" <BR>(name may change depending on how it turns out after I'm through with it.)<P>Currently named that because of it being nearly dead when I purchased it, and my ongoing restoration of it (it will rise from the dead to it's former glory).  Let me tell you, this car was trashed and barely ran....but I just couldn't let it end up in the boneyard.  It's my current daily driver until it starts to snow more. (it still has too many things wrong with it to list, but at least I've got it back to where it is semi-reliable.<P>Ken S.<BR>Western PA Fiero Club <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> <P>||||reg||1
