Z||000099||Fiero5||09-20-2001||08:17 PM||||Well, in the begining we used to refer to our ever growing collection as Fiero1, Fiero2 and so on due to the license plates. Now we have a few in the family that have broken that naming tradition like Slang and LVMY88.<BR>Marian is still trying to think of a name for hers. I call her Fiero "The Lean Mean Growling Machine". It's an 88 coupe so it has the lean nose look. It's also a notchback converted to a fastback 4 banger with a custom exhaust, that growls louder than most others we have ever been around.<P>My white 84SE "Fiero1" is my "Baby" as she was my first. My red 86SS we usually refer to as the red one or big red, or if a few of the other red ones are parked nearby we say The SS. Recently I have been refering to her as the Phoenix, as you can see from the pic below:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/The86SSPhoenix.jpg"> <P>Steve <P>------------------<BR>                                <IMG SRC="http://a1040.g.akamai.net/f/1040/759/1h/206.29.192.139/info/pics/sept11.jpg">                             <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||6
